{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 film directed by david fincher that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich, which chronicles the rise of mark zuckerberg and the consequences of his actions.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard, being dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rachelissa). in a fit of anger and hurt, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two harvard students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university.\n\nlater, mark is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are looking to create a social networking site for harvard students. they enlist the help of mark and his friend eduardo savernin (played by andrew garfield), but things quickly go sour as mark and eduardo start working on their own project, which they call \"thefacebook\".\n\nas thefacebook gains popularity, mark and eduardo become increasingly at odds over the direction of the company and their respective roles in it. meanwhile, the winklevoss brothers become angry when they realize that mark has stolen their idea and are determined to sue him for damages.\n\nthe film is known for its witty and engaging dialogue, which was written by aaron sorkin. the script is full of clever one-liners and insightful observations about the characters and their motivations. the cast delivers strong performances, with jesse eisenberg standing out as the complex and often unlikeable mark zuckerberg.\n\none of the strengths of the film is its ability to balance the personal and professional aspects of mark's life. we see him struggling to navigate his relationships with his friends and girlfriend, while also dealing with the pressures and challenges of building a successful business. the film also explores the themes of ambition, greed, and the consequences of one's actions.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy. it features a haunting and atmospheric soundtrack that perfectly captures the mood and tone of the film.\n\noverall, the social network is a thought-provoking and engaging film that is well worth watching. it's a fascinating look at the early days of facebook and the people who were involved in its creation. even if you're not familiar with the story, the film is still enjoyable as a character-driven drama that explores the complexities of human relationships and the consequences of our actions.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.9773347973823547}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -7.30726242181845e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.014163684099912643}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.7377774715423584}, {"token": "201", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0005864569102413952}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.0005529781919904053}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.1291094422340393}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.0009807306341826916}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.6689160474925302e-05}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -2.288792165927589e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0009114163694903255}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00020346954988781363}, {"token": " and